From: Peijin Zhang <peijin@ustc.edu>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:14:04 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Multiscale: transform the residual once per peak search,
 cache kernel FFTs

FindMultiScalePeak() convolved the residual with every scale kernel through
Convolve(), which transforms both the image and the kernel each time. The
residual is now transformed once for all scales and the transformed scale
kernels are cached per image size (bounded to 1 GiB), shared by clones.
Results are bitwise identical.

